lly. The bill text carries the provision quote.\n- **Why it seats no chair:**\n  1. At the federal level this topic is own words only, so no record can support a chair.\n  2. H.R. 5 is `multi-subject`: it also covers curriculum, budgets, library books and vaccines.\n  3. Its consent clause (section 401) covers changing a name or pronouns \"on any school form\". Rung 5 is about staff *using* a different name or pronouns, which is a different thing.\n- **`needs_source`:** Curtis's own words on whether schools should tell parents, or get their permission, when a student uses a different name or gender identity. That could be a statement, interview, questionnaire answer or explanation of his vote.\n\nThe labels file is `john-curtis/labels/coder-1.json`, under `backend/data/stance-research/2026-10-08-egi-a1v2/` in the worktree.","ttft_ms":8773,"type":"result","duration_ms":23718,"uuid":"c751b320-1a09-46cc-917e-73f94686bef2","ttft_stream_ms":1350,"time_to_request_ms":73,"first_content_frame_ms":1350,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
